  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:uppad_meaz" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n222.jpg">
        <tei:pb ed="1965" n="101" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n222.jpg"/>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:uppad_meaz/1"/>From of old has this day been appointed for judgment, for testing every day’s work; the creatures approach the countenance of the Awe-inspiring One that on it He may grant them a verdict of deliverance. <tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:uppad_meaz/2"/>On this day was the first man created; he received a law but did not keep it; on this day did he find a defender (in God) who helped him in need and appointed it a day of judgment to be maintained for later generations. <tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:uppad_meaz/3"/>On this day the hewn out foundations, the hills and the rocks, were formed for the sake of the first of the forefathers; and they, as dwellers in the garden (Eden) were present at the work of creation that on this day they might plead for those created. <tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:uppad_meaz/4"/>This day’s month bears the name of the immortals (forefathers); it is a sign for those above and below to assemble for the books to be opened, for deeds to be related and for men to pass by Thee and render account. <tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:uppad_meaz/5"/>This day was appointed first for the order of Thy festivals, and for the flock to be led under the staff past Thee; when Thy witnesses  <j:conditional xml:id="musaf_uppad_meaz_segment_6"><j:all><tei:fs type="opensiddur:holiday-aggregate"><tei:f name="shabbat"><tei:binary value="false"/></tei:f></tei:fs></j:all></j:conditional>blow <j:endConditional target="#musaf_uppad_meaz_segment_6"/><j:conditional type="marked" xml:id="musaf_uppad_meaz_segment_7"><j:all><tei:fs type="opensiddur:holiday-aggregate"><tei:f name="shabbat"><tei:binary value="true"/></tei:f></tei:fs></j:all></j:conditional>remember <j:endConditional target="#musaf_uppad_meaz_segment_7"/> the Shofar today, remember, O Merciful One, the oath of Thy servants. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:uppad_meaz/6"/>The sound of the Shofar rises with prayer, Almighty, to appease Thee with supplication; return the flashing sword to its sheath, grasp the shield that we may shelter beneath it. <tei:milestone unit="stanza"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
</tei:TEI>
